      "text": "We start by setting $x = 2,$ which yields $f(2) - 2 f \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 16.$ We can repeat this process $x$ times by setting $x = \\frac{1}{x},$ to get $f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) - 2f(2) = \\frac{1}{4},$ and $f\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) - 2f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{16},$ and $f\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) - 2f\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = \\frac{1}{64},$ and so on.\nRepeat this process $3$ times to get $f\\left(\\frac{1}{64}\\right) - 2f\\left(\\frac{1}{16}\\right) = \\frac{1}{4096}.$ We can combine these equations to get\n$f(2) - 2f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 16,$ $2f(2) - f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{4},$ $2f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) - f\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = \\frac{1}{16},$ $2f\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) - f\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{1}{64},$ $2f\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) - f\\left(\\frac{1}{16}\\right) = \\frac{1}{256},$\n$2f\\left(\\frac{1}{16}\\right) - f\\left(\\frac{1}{32}\\right) = \\frac{1}{1024},$ $2f\\left(\\frac{1}{32}\\right) - f\\left(\\frac{1}{64}\\right) = \\frac{3}{2048},$ and $2f\\left(\\frac{1}{64}\\right) - f(2) = \\frac{1}{4096}.$\nBy subtracting the first equation from the second, the second equation from the third, and so on, we get $f(2) = \\frac{49}{128}$ and $f(3) = \\frac{21}{32}.$\nTherefore, $f(2) = \\boxed{\\frac{49}{128}}.$. The answer is \\frac{49}{128}",
